Which license covers what
-------------------------

LICENSE (MIT) covers the program and the documentation written for it:

- src/
- the Gradle build: build.gradle.kts, settings.gradle.kts, gradle.properties,
  gradle/, gradlew, gradlew.bat
- config/experiment.json
- docs/js/, docs/css/, and docs/*.html
- README.md

MIT does not cover the SQuAD subset, or reproductions of its questions,
answers, or passages. Those are CC BY-SA 4.0. See data/LICENSE and
docs/data/NOTICE.

MIT does not cover model outputs under results/ (responses.jsonl, rationales,
scores). Copyright in model completions is unsettled, so this repository does
not grant it. See results/NOTICE.

Where a file mixes the two (for example a rationale that quotes a passage),
the quoted SQuAD or Wikipedia text stays under CC BY-SA 4.0.
